Indices given to these functions (\code{image}, \code{c}, \code{z}, \code{t}, \code{table}, \code{trace}, \code{sweep}, \code{run},
\code{index}, and the \code{x}, \code{y} of a \code{region}) start at 1, like R vectors. The metadata lists keep the
file's own numbering (\code{index}, \code{level}: from 0), and pyramid \code{level} 0 is full resolution.

Errors are conditions of class \code{openreadout_error} (and a specific class such as
\code{openreadout_corrupt_file} or \code{openreadout_unsupported_feature}) with fields \code{code},
\code{exit_code} and \code{hint}.

Options: \code{openreadout.tibble} (default \code{TRUE}: return tibbles when the tibble package is
installed), \code{openreadout.max_bytes} (default 4 GiB: the most memory \code{\link[=openreadout_read_image]{openreadout_read_image()}} may
allocate before asking for a selection, level or region).
